 "best_idea": "Derive the attack's length from one speed number, put the hit on the animation's hit frame as a share of that length (never less than half), add flight time from distance, and resolve the damage as a delayed command when it expires, so the clip, the projectile and the server hit share one clock.",
 "decision": "adapt",
 "decision_why": "Frankendom's duel step needs one attack clock with a per-creature hit frame as data; the donor's chain is a clean fit. But the donor lets hits overlap with no check and the client stretch relies on unverified Phaser semantics, so take the shape, add a per-hit ledger entry and a target re-check, and do not copy the overlap.",
 "decision_status": "proposed",
 "acceptance": "A server test with speed 100, hit frame 9 of 21 and a target 4 cells away asserts the hit resolves 1121 ms after the attack starts (455 ms wind-up, 667 ms flight); the client clip for that creature ends at 909 ms."
